From fccf71936f685c4ead09f9aaf36ef1edfc8beaef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 18:34:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add a per-provider uplink source address

A box with several uplinks, a local one and a tunnel per country, needs
each provider to leave through the right one: a Portuguese playlist over
the local line, an Italian one through the tunnel to Italy. Which uplink
a socket uses follows from the source address it is bound to, so this is
a routing decision the addon can make without any privilege.

The setting is per instance, so it is configured once per provider and
covers everything that provider does: every channel of its playlist, the
playlist and EPG downloads, and the connection check that gates them.
That check decides whether the client ever reports a connection, so a
provider whose uplink is up stays usable while another one's is down.
Nothing is expected of the M3U, which comes from the provider and knows
nothing about local interfaces.

A subnet or an interface name is resolved for each request rather than
stored, so a new DHCP lease does not strand the setting on an address
that no longer exists.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
